        "explanation": "Historically, there were many ways (`.bind()`, `.live()`, `.delegate()`). \nHowever, since jQuery 1.7, the single, unified, and correct way to bind an event is using the **`.on()`** method. Shorthand methods like `.click()` and `.keyup()` still exist, but they are just wrappers that call `.on()` under the hood.",
