        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "Event delegation is a technique where, instead of attaching an event listener to individual child elements, you attach ONE single event listener to a static parent element. \nWhen a child is clicked, the event 'bubbles up' to the parent. The parent then checks if the element that triggered the event matches a specific selector, and if so, executes the code.",
