        "explanation": "Event bubbling is a core mechanism of the browser's DOM. When an event (like a click) occurs on an element, it first triggers on that specific element, and then it **bubbles up** through its ancestors in the HTML tree, triggering click events on every parent all the way up to the `document` root.",
