        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The Same-Origin Policy (SOP) is the most fundamental security model of the web. \nIt states that a web browser permits scripts contained in a first web page to access data in a second web page ONLY if both web pages have the exact same **Origin**. \nAn Origin is defined by three things matching exactly: **Protocol** (`http` vs `https`), **Port** (`80` vs `443`), and **Host/Domain** (`google.com`).",
