        "title": "What is ajaxStart()?",
        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "`ajaxStart()` is a global event that fires when an AJAX request begins, **AND** there are currently no other AJAX requests running. \nIt signifies the exact moment the application transitions from an idle state to a 'network active' state.",
        "example": "Disabling the UI.",
