        "id": 120,
        "title": "What is ajaxStop()?",
        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "`ajaxStop()` is a global event that fires when **ALL** active AJAX requests have completely finished. \nIt signifies the exact moment the application transitions back to a completely idle state.",
