        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "`ajaxSend()` is a global event that fires every single time an AJAX request is about to be sent. \nUnlike `ajaxStart` (which only fires for the very first request in a batch), `ajaxSend` fires for *every* individual request. This makes it the perfect place to globally inject headers (like CSRF tokens) into every request your app makes.",
