        "id": 126,
        "title": "How do you upload files using AJAX?",
        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "File uploads cannot be sent as standard URL-encoded text. They must be sent as binary data using the `multipart/form-data` encoding. \nTo do this via AJAX, you must use the native JavaScript `FormData` object to package the file, and you must explicitly tell jQuery **NOT** to process the data and **NOT** to set a content type (allowing the browser to handle the complex boundaries automatically).",
