        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "If a server crashes or the user's internet drops, an AJAX request might hang in a 'pending' state indefinitely, freezing the UI. \nYou must set a `timeout` (in milliseconds). If the request takes longer than this limit, jQuery automatically aborts the request and fires the `error` callback with the status `'timeout'`.",
