        "explanation": "If a page needs data from 3 different API endpoints, running them sequentially (waiting for A to finish, then starting B) is incredibly slow. \nYou optimize this by running them concurrently (in parallel) and waiting for all of them to finish before rendering the UI. In jQuery, this is done using `$.when()`.",
