        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "AJAX polling (specifically short polling) is a technique used to simulate real-time data updates. \nBecause the server cannot 'push' data to the browser via AJAX, the client writes a `setInterval` loop that blindly sends an AJAX request to the server every X seconds asking, 'Is there any new data?'.",
