        "id": 134,
        "title": "What is long polling?",
        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "Long polling is a much smarter version of polling that reduces wasted bandwidth. \nThe client sends an AJAX request. If the server has no new data, the server does **NOT** respond immediately. It holds the connection open (often for up to 30 seconds). The moment new data arrives on the server, it responds. The client receives the data, processes it, and instantly opens a new long-polling request.",
        "example": "The architecture.",
        "code": "// Recursive Long Polling\nfunction longPoll() {\n    $.ajax({\n        url: '/api/chat/wait-for-message',\n        timeout: 30000, // Wait up to 30s before aborting\n        success: function(data) {\n            updateChatUI(data);\n        },\n        complete: function() {\n            // As soon as it finishes (success or timeout), instantly ask again\n            longPoll(); \n        }\n    });\n}\nlongPoll();",
