        "explanation": "- **AJAX (HTTP):** Half-duplex. Client requests, Server responds. The connection closes. Every request carries heavy HTTP header overhead (cookies, user-agents). Ideal for standard CRUD operations.\n- **WebSockets (WS):** Full-duplex. A single connection stays open forever. Both client and server can send messages at any time. Zero HTTP header overhead per message. Ideal for multiplayer games, stock tickers, and live chat.",
        "example": "When to use which.",
