        "explanation": "Server-Sent Events (SSE) is a web standard built specifically for unidirectional (one-way) real-time data flow from the Server to the Client over standard HTTP. \nIt acts like a never-ending AJAX response. The client opens a connection via the native `EventSource` API, and the server continuously streams text data down the pipe.",
