        "explanation": "AJAX applications are inherently exposed to the internet. Security involves:\n1. **HTTPS / TLS:** Always use HTTPS so data payloads (especially passwords) are encrypted in transit.\n2. **Authentication:** Use secure HTTP-only cookies or Bearer Tokens (JWT) for every request.\n3. **CORS:** Properly configure backend CORS headers to only accept requests from your exact frontend domain.\n4. **Input Sanitization:** Never trust client data; validate and sanitize all AJAX payloads on the backend to prevent SQL Injection.",
