        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "1. **XSS (Cross-Site Scripting):** An attacker injects malicious JS into the database. When AJAX fetches it and renders it via `.html()`, it executes and steals user data.\n2. **CSRF (Cross-Site Request Forgery):** A malicious site tricks the user's browser into quietly sending an unauthorized AJAX POST request to your bank/app while they are logged in.\n3. **Data Exposure:** Returning a massive JSON object with hidden passwords or admin flags, assuming the frontend simply won't display them.",
