        "explanation": "Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) exploits how browsers automatically attach session cookies to requests. \nIf you are logged into `bank.com`, and visit `evil.com`, `evil.com` can run a hidden script that makes a POST request to `bank.com/transfer`. The browser automatically attaches your Bank cookies, and the server thinks YOU authorized the transfer.",
