        "title": "How do you pass authentication tokens in AJAX?",
        "category": "Advanced AJAX, Performance, Security & Architecture",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "In modern stateless architectures, authentication is usually handled via tokens (like JWT). \nTokens should **never** be passed in the URL query string. They must be passed securely in the HTTP Headers, specifically using the `Authorization` header with the `Bearer` schema.",
