        "explanation": "API Rate Limiting is a defense mechanism used by servers to prevent abuse. It restricts how many AJAX requests a single user (or IP address) can make within a certain timeframe (e.g., 60 requests per minute). \nIf you exceed this, the server stops processing your requests and returns an HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) status code.",
