        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "A polyfill is a piece of code (usually JavaScript on the Web) used to provide modern functionality on older browsers that do not natively support it. \nThe native `fetch()` API was introduced in ES6. Older browsers like Internet Explorer 11 do not understand `fetch()`. If you write `fetch()` without a polyfill, the app crashes in IE11.",
