        "category": "Bonus: Advanced AJAX & Edge Cases",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "When a user closes a browser tab, you often want to send a final analytics event (like 'time spent on page'). \nIf you use `$.ajax()` inside the `window.onunload` event, the browser will likely cancel the network request to close the tab faster. The `navigator.sendBeacon()` API was created specifically for this. It schedules a small asynchronous POST request that the browser guarantees will finish in the background, even after the tab is fully closed.",
