        "explanation": "Because `$.ajax()` returns a Promise (jqXHR), it is fully compatible with modern ES8 `async/await` syntax. \nTo run requests concurrently (in parallel) and wait for all of them, you use `Promise.all()`. This is the modern, vastly superior replacement for jQuery's `$.when()`.",
