        "explanation": "Instead of binding a costly `scroll` event listener to trigger infinite loading, modern development uses the `IntersectionObserver`. \nYou place an empty HTML `<div>` at the bottom of the page. You tell the Observer to watch it. When the browser calculates that the `<div>` has scrolled into view on the screen, it fires a callback to trigger the AJAX request. This requires zero math and zero scroll events.",
