        "category": "Bonus: Advanced AJAX & Edge Cases",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "The 'Thundering Herd' problem occurs when thousands of connected clients all fire an AJAX polling request to the server at the exact same millisecond, instantly overloading the database and crashing the server. \nThis happens if a server reboots and 10,000 clients all reconnect simultaneously with a strict `setInterval(poll, 5000)`.",
        "example": "Adding 'Jitter' to prevent crashes.",
