        "title": "Describe how a Service Worker handles offline POST requests (Background Sync API).",
        "category": "Bonus: Advanced AJAX & Edge Cases",
        "language": "javascript",
        "explanation": "If a user is offline and submits a form via AJAX (POST), it will fail. \nThe Background Sync API allows a Service Worker to intercept that failed POST request, save the payload into the browser's IndexedDB, and register a 'Sync' event. The moment the mobile device detects an internet connection (even if the browser is closed!), the Service Worker wakes up and executes the POST request to the server.",
